00:21:26.551 --> 00:21:28.420 align:start position:0%
Other than that,
it did pretty well.

00:21:28.453 --> 00:21:29.921 align:start size:66% position:34%
I feel like we proved

00:21:29.954 --> 00:21:32.590 align:start size:69% position:31%
the original use case
for the Sport Walkman.

00:21:32.623 --> 00:21:34.926 align:start size:81% position:19%
Running, jogging--
obviously performed great.

00:21:34.959 --> 00:21:36.895 align:start position:0%
Yeah, got to give
props to certain aspects
of the Walkman

00:21:36.928 --> 00:21:38.096 align:start size:69% position:31%
for holding up
better than I thought.

00:21:38.129 --> 00:21:39.631 align:start position:0%
Thank you, guys,
for helping me

00:21:39.664 --> 00:21:41.066
- test out the Walkman.
- Thanks for having us.

00:21:41.099 --> 00:21:42.801 align:start position:0%
The Gregory Brothers.

00:21:42.834 --> 00:21:44.502
So the Sports Walkman
actually held up pretty well,

00:21:44.535 --> 00:21:46.438
but it was just one example

00:21:46.471 --> 00:21:50.008 line:0%
of Sony's effort to appeal
to people's unique interests.

00:21:50.041 --> 00:21:51.976 line:0%
Lisa: They launched
different colors.

00:21:52.009 --> 00:21:55.447 line:0%
They eventually launched a model
that also had AM and FM.

00:21:55.480 --> 00:22:00.085 line:0%
Americus:
By giving consumers enough
variation in the product SKUs,

00:22:00.118 --> 00:22:02.454 line:0%
that allowed them to say,
"I still feel like

00:22:02.487 --> 00:22:04.022
this product is personal to me

00:22:04.055 --> 00:22:06.358 line:0%
even though everyone has one."

00:22:06.391 --> 00:22:07.959 line:0%
Marques:
Through the mid-1980s

00:22:07.992 --> 00:22:09.494 line:7%
and into the early '90s,

00:22:09.527 --> 00:22:11.496 line:0%
the Walkman had firmly
established itself

00:22:11.529 --> 00:22:14.966 line:0%
as a cultural icon,
often taking on starring roles

00:22:14.999 --> 00:22:17.001 line:0%
in classic movies of the era.

00:22:17.034 --> 00:22:20.138 line:0%
♪ Leave it all up to me ♪

00:22:20.171 --> 00:22:22.807 line:0%
Marques: But by the time
Sony celebrated

00:22:22.840 --> 00:22:24.976 line:0%
the Walkman's
tenth anniversary,

00:22:25.009 --> 00:22:27.479 line:0%
a new frontier of technology
was on the horizon.

00:22:29.680 --> 00:22:31.116
Lisa:
Technology always evolves,

00:22:31.149 --> 00:22:32.584
and the way we listen to music

00:22:32.617 --> 00:22:34.652
and get music always changes.

00:22:34.685 --> 00:22:36.521
Alex:
Once we got towards
the middle of the '90s,

00:22:36.554 --> 00:22:39.691
the medium of a compact disc
was able to hold more.

00:22:39.724 --> 00:22:42.093
The sound was a lot more hi-fi.

00:22:42.126 --> 00:22:45.029
Lisa:
As CD players rose
in popularity,

00:22:45.062 --> 00:22:48.833
you kind of saw the appeal
of the Walkman start to fade.

00:22:48.866 --> 00:22:51.136
And what really marked
the end of the Walkman was,

00:22:51.169 --> 00:22:53.805
of course, the iPod in 2001.

00:22:53.838 --> 00:22:57.142
Now you can have
your entire music library
in your pocket,

00:22:57.175 --> 00:23:00.111
not just one or two cassettes
of your choosing.

00:23:00.144 --> 00:23:02.147
So, it was really
digital music

00:23:02.180 --> 00:23:04.583
that put the nail
in the coffin for the Walkman.

00:23:06.717 --> 00:23:09.687 align:start size:81% position:19%
Can you just give me
the legacy of the Walkman?

00:23:09.720 --> 00:23:11.856
Americus:
It's the first time
that you saw music

00:23:11.889 --> 00:23:14.159
really stepping outside
of the background

00:23:14.192 --> 00:23:16.861
and into the forefront
as a very central

00:23:16.894 --> 00:23:19.130
means of self-expression
for consumers.

00:23:19.163 --> 00:23:21.533
The Walkman kind of
created this notion

00:23:21.566 --> 00:23:23.768
that technology can be
with you all the time.

00:23:23.801 --> 00:23:26.671
Today, we don't leave
the house without our phones.

00:23:26.704 --> 00:23:29.874
We spend hundreds of dollars
on specialized headphones

00:23:29.907 --> 00:23:32.143
because we love them and want to
wear them all the time.

00:23:32.176 --> 00:23:34.712
The Walkman was so critical
in all of that.

00:23:34.745 --> 00:23:37.882 line:0%
The Walkman is still seen
in pop culture today.

00:23:37.915 --> 00:23:40.051 line:0%
I mean, think about
"Guardians Of The Galaxy,"

00:23:40.084 --> 00:23:43.755 line:0%
which was a hugely popular movie
in the Marvel franchise.

00:23:43.788 --> 00:23:45.723
So, it definitely got
a little bit of a revival.

00:23:45.756 --> 00:23:47.192
Seth:
If you're listening
to a Walkman,

00:23:47.225 --> 00:23:48.726
or nowadays an iPhone,

00:23:48.759 --> 00:23:50.061
while you're
going about your day,

00:23:50.094 --> 00:23:52.197
it changes your relationship
with the world.

00:23:52.230 --> 00:23:54.065
It makes it much easier
to get through the day,

00:23:54.098 --> 00:23:56.468
whether you're working a job
or working out.

00:23:56.501 --> 00:23:58.736
The Walkman allowed us
for the first time

00:23:58.769 --> 00:24:00.238
to be transported away.

00:24:00.271 --> 00:24:02.073
It changed everything about

00:24:02.106 --> 00:24:04.643
how music fits into our lives.

00:24:06.244 --> 00:24:08.079
Marques:
I've learned a lot

00:24:08.112 --> 00:24:10.114
from my time
with the original Walkman.

00:24:10.147 --> 00:24:12.083
The biggest takeaway for me

00:24:12.116 --> 00:24:14.486
is just how much
this thing paved the way

00:24:14.519 --> 00:24:17.989 align:start position:0% line:0%
for portable audio
as we know it today.

00:24:18.022 --> 00:24:22.560 align:start position:0% line:0%
From the gears inside,
to the bands, to the buttons--

00:24:22.593 --> 00:24:24.963 line:0%
those amazing clicky buttons,

00:24:24.996 --> 00:24:26.931 align:start position:0% line:0%
they don't make 'em
like they used to.

00:24:26.964 --> 00:24:29.901 align:start position:0% line:0%
So, thanks to
the Walkman,

00:24:29.934 --> 00:24:32.604 size:84% position:42% line:0%
and thank you for watching.

00:24:32.637 --> 00:24:34.506 align:start position:0% line:0%
Catch you guys
in the next one. Peace.

